When a HTTP call results in an error, it doesnât signal the error in the usual way, so we canât use [protected evaluation](../../ref/apply/#trap) to trap the error. Rather, it generates a HTTP response displaying the error. HTTP/1.1 400 Bad Request
    Content-Type: text/plain
