We can see that after blocking listener 1, the next two connections were allocated to listener 2. As listener 2âs main thread was not blocked, these messages were processed immediately. The following connection attempt was routed to listener 1, which was blocked. Due to the process being busy, the client hangs until this connection is established. When the listener was no longer blocked, the connection was established and messages continue to be processed as normal.

